ross those loads. Bootstrap selection uses existing applicable constraints: default unified-v2 inputs, the npm 230 ms ceiling, retained floors, successful outcomes and clean final memory. No PyPI ceiling existed during sample selection. The new PyPI ceiling is derived after selection and governs future observations. Recorded maxima can exceed that ceiling because the formula uses the lowest per-shape maximum. The original npm maxima keep their historical source group and are not recomputed from these new observations. The new PyPI maxima use only the final three qualifying runs. Each ecosystem uses the same ceiling formula independently because its floors depend on its own injected RTT. Runs 38502988119 and 38513015540 are wholly excluded because a profile exceeded the existing npm ceiling. They contribute no counts or latency maxima. Failures and adverse observations remain in the corresponding workflow reports. Future runs above either applicable native ceiling are unheld as a whole. The 3cpu-1gib and 3cpu-2gib floors replace the 4cpu-1gib and 4cpu-2gib floors, which are removed with every cell and latency maximum they held. The final six run records are single-shape dispatches at bc1318504a8d1d1b5a354e82ca474dc07c7506bb with default unified-v2 settings: 39898414830, 39926368840 and 39939530905 for 3cpu-1gib, and 39898474741, 39906019751 and 39908529268 for 3cpu-2gib. Each 3cpu floor is half the lowest count over its shape's three runs, rounded down, and at least 1. The same runs supply the 3cpu latency maxima. Both ceilings are derived again over the four pod shapes: npm falls from 230 ms to 180 ms, and PyPI stays at 20 ms. Ten other dispatched runs on the same commit are wholly excluded because a profile injected PyPI latency above 20 ms: 39888028214, 39889214660, 39889244349, 39889263094, 39898435819, 39898455317, 39905999618, 39914098037, 39919944930 and 39932840636. retainedFloorConditions describes the unlimited and 2cpu-1gib rows only. Every 3cpu row is measured under unified-v2.",
